{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5i3C3jR44KJoU27ivfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw domain exceptions (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts exceptions to ApiError responses\n- Error codes in ErrorCode enum define the error contract\n- Tests use MockMvc with status() and jsonPath() matchers\n- Repository returns null for not-found items (caller handles 404)\n- Services directly use repositories, no additional layers\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - add new error code for CANCELLED shipment case\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - add POST confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for all 4 cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Error code naming convention (must follow existing patterns)\n- Idempotent behavior on already-CONFIRMED shipments (must persist correctly)\n- Test must properly set up CANCELLED shipment (direct repo write)\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The requirement is clear: CREATED→CONFIRMED moves state, CONFIRMED stays CONFIRMED, CANCELLED rejects with 409, missing ID returns 404.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This follows the pattern of existing codes like `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` and accurately describes the conflicting state.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a POST endpoint `confirm` at path `/{shipmentId}/confirm`. The endpoint will:\n   - Accept a shipment ID path variable\n   - Fetch the shipment; if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` (404)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED via `repository.save()` and return it with 200\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return it unchanged with 200 (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with code `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` (409)\n   - Return the shipment as JSON\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` - creates S-confirm, confirms it, verifies status is CONFIRMED\n   - `confirms a shipment idempotently when already confirmed` - creates S-idempotent, confirms twice, verifies both succeed and status remains CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` - uses repo to directly insert a CANCELLED shipment, attempts confirm, expects 409 and `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` code\n   - `rejects confirming unknown shipment with 404` - attempts confirm on non-existent ID, expects 404 and `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered whether to use a generic status code like `VALIDATION_FAILED` for the CANCELLED case, but that's semantically incorrect (it's not a validation failure, it's a state conflict). I also considered not adding a new error code and reusing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, but that would be confusing. The chosen approach of a dedicated `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` code is explicit, consistent with the codebase pattern, and provides clear error semantics.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | Find by ID (not null) | `save(Shipment with CONFIRMED)` | 200 with shipment JSON | Repository.save() returns updated entity |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | Find by ID (not null) | `save(Shipment with CONFIRMED)` | 200 with shipment JSON | Repository.save() called but state unchanged |\n| CANCELLED | Find by ID (not null) | None | 409 + ApiError | ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Not found | None (null) | None | 404 + ApiError | ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 covers \"confirms a created shipment and persists it\" (acceptance criterion 3)\n- Test 2 covers \"a repeated confirm succeeds\" (acceptance criterion 5)\n- Test 3 covers \"a cancelled shipment is refused\" (acceptance criterion 5)\n- Test 4 covers \"an unknown id is refused\" (acceptance criterion 5)\n- All tests verify error responses use the ApiError envelope (acceptance criterion 4)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me now implement the three file changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2001,"cache_read_input_tokens":17156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2001},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"256bd4cf-b18e-4d7b-851f-2e61b6fe1c1e","uuid":"38c7a086-61b4-4a4e-8d22-4a793f226975","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:36:10.729Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5i3BZxsE1QdpirrQkBw"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5i3C3jR44KJoU27ivfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MhtYzARTkaTDVnj6KS1eUW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c1d3bebf-6cfc-4e93-9d93-6ed56768cfeb/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt","old_string":"/**\n * The closed set of machine-readable error codes. Clients switch on these, so a code is\n * part of the public API: add one deliberately, never rename one casually.\n */\nenum class ErrorCode {\n    ORDER_NOT_FOUND,\n    ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    VALIDATION_FAILED,\n}","new_string":"/**\n * The closed set of machine-readable error codes. Clients switch on these, so a code is\n * part of the public API: add one deliberately, never rename one casually.\n */\nenum class ErrorCode {\n    ORDER_NOT_FOUND,\n    ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED,\n    VALIDATION_FAILED,\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2001,"cache_read_input_tokens":17156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2001},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"256bd4cf-b18e-4d7b-851f-2e61b6fe1c1e","uuid":"65d4b162-7931-49ed-9f56-6878ea9877d7","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:36:14.643Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5i3BZxsE1QdpirrQkBw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MhtYzARTkaTDVnj6KS1eUW":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c1d3bebf-6cfc-4e93-9d93-6ed56768cfeb/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityin