ry because the confirm endpoint needs an error code for the conflict case.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added `confirm` method (25 lines added), updated class comment. The method:\n   - Uses `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` following Spring conventions\n   - Fetches shipment with 404 handling (ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - Uses Kotlin `when` expression to handle three status cases\n   - CREATED case: saves updated shipment with CONFIRMED status\n   - CONFIRMED case: returns shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - CANCELLED case: throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED code\n   - All error paths use existing exception types handled by GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 new test methods (40 lines added), updated class comment:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` - verifies status transition CREATED → CONFIRMED\n   - `confirms a shipment idempotently when already confirmed` - verifies retry succeeds and status unchanged\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` - sets up CANCELLED shipment, expects 409 and correct error code\n   - `rejects confirming unknown shipment with 404` - expects 404 and correct error code\n   - All tests follow existing MockMvc pattern with status() and jsonPath() matchers\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. The implementation is complete and all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint to confirm a shipment, moving from CREATED to CONFIRMED, handling retries idempotently, rejecting CANCELLED with 409, and unknown IDs with 404.\nChanged       ApiError.kt: added SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED error code\n              ShipmentController.kt: added confirm endpoint with status-based logic\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: added 4 tests covering confirm, idempotency, cancelled rejection, and not-found cases\nTests         confirms a created shipment - CREATED→CONFIRMED transition\n  